{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>They have provoked Me to jealousy.</b> They kindled My wrath." "<b>With a no-god.</b> With a thing that is not a god." "<b>With a no-people.</b> With a nation that has no name, as it is said (Isaiah 23) ״הֵן אֶרֶץ כַּשְׂדִים זֶה הָעָם לֹא הָיָה״; of Esau He says (Obadiah 1) ״בָּזוּי אַתָּה מְאֹד״." "<b>With a vile nation I will provoke them to anger.</b> These are the sectarians, and so He says (Psalms 14) ״אָמַר נָבָל בְּלִבּוֹ אֵין אֱלֹהִים״ (Sifrei; Yevamot 63)."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:49:20.711408025Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}